<p>Say: Why does this matter for policy? A policy is judged by what it changes in what people can do.
The model measures this as accessibility, in yen: the value of all the days a person can still live.
So it is only right if each person's possible days are right. Shops open until nine: without
constraints, the parent gains nothing; with them, the parent gains. Wrong constraints give wrong
winners and losers.</p>
